## Context

After useful delivery exists, add optional editorial support on the strong host. Candidate grouping is not generalisation, and rediscovery creates only an opportunity.

Design baseline: v6, merged by PR #903. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Dreaming skill; library corpus reader; pilot/available shared inputs; review/provenance conventions.

## Actions

1. Propose lexical candidate groups and possible contradictions with source UUID/revisions. Do not prescribe harness-copy survival or project-copy retirement.
2. Hand candidates to 0916; empty output or no change is valid. A false-positive fixture may be proposed but must never be represented as already judged equivalent.
3. Record useful operational diagnostics without a new mandatory rejection database. If dismissed candidates need suppression, use existing review provenance keyed by source revisions, not an eternal pair ban.
4. Keep editorial analysis separate from publication; perform no canonical writes in this ticket.

## Test

Known related observations are surfaced; differently scoped near-matches retain their distinct evidence. Repeating a discovery changes no lifecycle or scope. Pending/rejected proposals cannot block compiler output.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v6, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Candidate interface is reviewable and UUID/revision-addressed.
- [ ] No synthesis, automatic scope expansion, tombstoning or lock-based global coordination.
- [ ] No embedding or quality-backfill prerequisite.
